// Negative control OWED BY THE LANE: the envelope-plus-sidecar total.
//
// A crossing plan sizes a payload as fixed envelope/header bytes plus the
// payload's own storage plus any typed sidecar, and that sum has its own
// overflow. The arithmetic does not exist yet — `internal/layout` computes type
// layouts only, and the envelope/sidecar totals belong to the transport work
// that follows ordinary storage — so there is nothing for this source to trip
// today and the harness row is skipped with that reason rather than asserted.
//
// The shape is recorded here so the row has a home the moment the arithmetic
// lands: a composite large enough that its envelope total is what overflows
// rather than the type itself. Until then this file must compile cleanly; a
// diagnostic from it today would mean something else is wrong.

@align(4294967296)
type Wide = { value: bool };

type NearLimitPayload = {
    bulk: Wide[4294967294],
};

@entrypoint
fn main() -> int {
    return 0;
}
